# Implementation Flow

## Purpose

Record the ordered process for <strong>{{PROJECT_NAME}}</strong> when stage order, timing, validation gates, artifact handoffs, failure boundaries, or recovery points form part of the project contract.

Keep component responsibilities, dependencies, and call relationships in `CODE_ARCHITECTURE.en.md`. Remove this optional document if it only repeats that file.

## Active identity

- <strong>Process, version, or method identity:</strong> Unconfirmed during initialization.
- <strong>Lifecycle:</strong> `unconfirmed` until supported by user confirmation or project evidence.
- <strong>Evidence authority:</strong> `reference-only` until the active identity and validity boundary are confirmed.
- <strong>Validity boundary:</strong> Confirm the inputs, outputs, and effective version before relying on this flow.

## End-to-end flow

```text
confirmed input
  -> stage or transformation
       -> validation gate
       -> retained artifact
  -> next stage
       -> handoff or recovery point
  -> confirmed output
```

Replace the generic flow only with inspected behavior or explicit user confirmation.

